title: "NZ-OCDS Mapping: A draft New Zealand implementation profile for the Open Contracting Data Standard"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
version: "0.4"
date-released: "2026-05-07"
authors:
  - family-names: Walker-Tepania
    given-names: Manaaki
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
url: "https://github.com/manwaltep/nz-ocds-mapping"
abstract: >
  A draft New Zealand implementation profile for the Open Contracting
  Data Standard (OCDS). Cross-references 114 OCDS 1.1.5 paths against
  publicly available Government Electronic Tenders Service (GETS) data,
  the NZ Government Procurement Rules (5th edition, 2025), and the
  NZGP Approved Government Model Templates. Proposes 18 NZ-specific
  extensions, each anchored to a specific Procurement Rule and
  glossary entry. Prepared as evidence that NZ's OGP commitment NZ0029
  to OCDS alignment is technically feasible substantially ahead of
  the current 2030 timeline.
